 "issue": 313,
 "issue_title": "Three divergent `WavefrontSensor` / `PSFCalculator` implementations; the optimizer's MTF merit uses the wrong one",
 "issue_body": "**Files:** `src/optimizer.py:19` vs `src/analysis/__init__.py:4` vs `openlens.py:41`\n\n`src.optimizer` and `src.analysis.__init__` import from `beam_synthesis`; `openlens.py:41` imports\nfrom `diffraction_psf`. The implementations differ **physically**:\n\n- `diffraction_psf.py:166-179` removes piston **and tilt** via a least-squares plane fit and\n  references a real sphere through the chief ray.\n- `beam_synthesis.py:205-209` removes **piston only** and references a flat plane at\n  `ref_ray.path[-1].x`.\n\n`MeritFunction._eval_mtf` (`optimizer.py:188-197`) therefore scores the MTF of a **tilt-contaminated**\nwavefront. At any nonzero field the pupil function carries a linear phase ramp, the PSF smears\nacross the padded window, and the MTF is dominated by field angle rather than aberration.\n\n**Fix:** delete `beam_synthesis.WavefrontSensor` and `beam_synthesis.PSFCalculator`; import the\n`diffraction_psf` pair everywhere (they supersede them: `pad_factor`, NaN masking, tilt removal,\nreference sphere).\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/313",
 "pr": 420,
 "pr_title": "refactor(analysis): one wavefront/PSF implementation, and it removes tilt",
 "pr_body": "Closes #313\n\n## Two implementations, different physics\n\n| | `diffraction_psf` | `beam_synthesis` |\n|---|---|---|\n| reference | real sphere through the chief ray | flat plane at `ref_ray.path[-1].x` |\n| piston removed | yes | yes |\n| **tilt removed** | **yes** (least-squares plane fit) | **no** |\n| padding / NaN mask | yes | no |\n\n`psf_mtf`, `aberrations` and `openlens` already used the good one. Only `optimizer._eval_mtf` used the other.\n\n## Measured residual tilt in the returned wavefront\n\n```\nfield      beam_synthesis (removed)   diffraction_psf (survivor)\n  0 deg           -5e-14                      -5e-15\n  5 deg       -1.84e+02                      +4e-14\n 10 deg       -3.80e+02                      -2e-13\n```\n\nSo the MTF merit was scoring a wavefront carrying a **184-wave linear phase ramp** at 5\u00b0. That ramp smears the PSF across the padded window \u2014 the merit was measuring **field angle, not aberration**, and the optimizer was being driven by it.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe two divergent classes are deleted. `GaussianBeam` and `BeamSynthesisPropagator` stay \u2014 Gaussian beam synthesis is a separate, still-valid feature. `analysis.__init__` and `optimizer` both name `diffraction_psf` explicitly, so there is now **one** object rather than two that can drift again. `analysis.__init__` no longer exports the ambiguous name `PSFCalculator`.\n\n## Bonus: numpy degradation\n\n`diffraction_psf` imported numpy unguarded, and `openlens.py` imports `WavefrontSensor` from it at module scope \u2014 so the app could not start without numpy, contradicting AGENTS.md's rule that numpy is optional. With the guard, `src.optimizer` and `src.analysis` import cleanly without numpy and the MTF merit returns `INFEASIBLE_MERIT`. The one remaining GUI blocker is `gui/dialogs/analysis_plots.py` \u2014 **#311's** territory, already fixed in PR #388.\n\n## Tests\n\n15 new tests: the deleted names are gone, the survivor is exported, all four consumers resolve to the *same* class object, residual tilt is ~1e-14 at 0\u00b0/5\u00b0/10\u00b0, a genuine quadratic defocus survives the plane fit intact (so tilt removal isn't quietly flattening real aberration), the MTF merit is finite, and the Airy-pattern assertions dropped from `test_beam_synthesis.TestPSF` are preserved against the survivor \u2014 with `pad_factor=4` rather than the removed copy's 2.\n\nOne of my own tests was wrong and I removed it: I asserted that constructing a `WavefrontError` with a linear ramp would strip it. `WavefrontError` is a plain holder; the fit happens inside the sensor.\n",
